0result.sql
```

0result.sql is both correct and the most straightforward:

• It calculates each player’s match‑runs, filters for totals ≥ 100, and uses the same Ball‑by‑Ball rows to know which team the batsman was batting for (team_batting).  
• It then simply compares that team_id with match.match_winner to keep only centuries scored for the losing side.  
• No extra joins (e.g., to player_match) or CTEs are needed, so the query is shorter and easier to read while still returning the exact required list of player names.